#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""edr-bans: apply the agent's ban state to nftables (client PLAN section 4.2).

A small root oneshot with fixed input and output. The unprivileged agent decides, this program
applies. It trusts nothing it reads: /run/edr-agent/bans.json belongs to the agent, which may be
compromised, so every field is checked, the never-ban literals are compiled in, and the nft
script is built only from str(ipaddress.ip_network(...)) and integers.

Input   /run/edr-agent/bans.json   (agent, hostile)
        /etc/edr-agent/pause.json  (root, {"until": epoch})    while valid: ban and feed sets are emptied
        /etc/edr-agent/local.conf  ([bans] bigconn_bytes, bigconn_cap; [sites] web_users)
        /var/lib/edr-bans/state.json   the last good state, absolute expiries
Output  table inet edr (nft -c, then nft -f: one atomic replace)
        /var/lib/edr-bans/state.json, /run/edr-bans/counters.json, /run/edr-bans/applied.json

Usage   edr-bans [--root DIR] [--dry-run] [--print-script] [--files-dir DIR] [--now EPOCH]
        --root DIR       prefix every path with DIR (also EDR_AGENT_ROOT); tests and dev runs
        --dry-run        do not call nft; print the script; files are still written under --root
        --print-script   print the nft script for the current bans.json and exit; writes nothing
Python standard library only, run as: python3 -I edr-bans
"""

